<h1>depth</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Of a <a href="node.html"><em>node</em></a>, the distance from the node to the <a href="root.html"><em>root</em></a> of the <a href="tree.html"><em>tree</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Formal Definition:</strong> The depth of the root is 0.  The depth of a node is one plus the depth of its <a href="parent.html"><em>parent</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Aggregate parent</strong> (I am a part of or used in ...)<br>
<a href="tree.html"><em>tree</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="height.html"><em>height</em></a>, <a href="level.html"><em>level</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
For instance, the root has or is at depth 0, and a <a href="child.html"><em>child</em></a> of the root has or is at depth 1.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

